set verbose off

# Usage:
open nels.gdt --quiet
include BACE.gfn

# We specify list of explanatory variables
list X = 2..14

# We set the seed in order to exact reproduction of results
set seed 1000000

set stopwatch
BACE(psechoice, X, _(model_type="probit"))
printf "Total execution time: %.2f sec.\n", $stopwatch
/*
Suppose we want to run ordered logit instead of probit analysis.
What's more, we want to use Beta-Binomial prior over model size
and perform jointness analysis using modified Yule's Q Measure.
W'd like to switch off ploting grahs. Finally, we also want to save
results of the BACE analysis under thr RES bundle:
*/
RES = BACE(psechoice, X, _(model_type="logit", model_prior="beta-binomial",\
 do_joint="MYQ", do_plot=0))
printf "Total execution time: %.2f sec.\n", $stopwatch
/*
Suppose we want to calculate Doppelhofer-Weeks Measure instead of
already computed Ley-Steel Measure. Since the type of jointness measure
is controlled by do_join field in the result bundle, the only thing
we have to do is to set the value of do_join to 2 and print BACE
results again. The code should be as follows:
*/
RES["do_joint"] = 1
BACE_Print(&RES)
